knowledge-is-a-lack-of-ignorance-3 = unlines (cons (quoted (cons "" (cons "Knowledge is a lack of ignorance" (cons " (Avik, 2026-11-15) is the Greek definition of truth. *A-lētheia* is not-forgetting: truth is defined by negating the forgetting. *Ignorance* is *in-* + *gnarus*, not-knowing, the same root as *knowledge* (*ǵneh₃-*, Greek *gnōsis*). So knowledge as the absence of ignorance makes knowing the ground state, with ignorance as what gets added on top. That is Avik's original clarity (his thesis that knowledge is a descent into ignorance from an original clarity, to be unlearned and remembered), and it's why the process that builds fields of knowledge is an ignorance process." nil)))) nil)
